a=s.index("## What a used household object is here"); b=s.index("## What an asset document is")
s=s[:a]+'''## What a used instrument is here

A second-hand musical instrument or piece of music equipment as a used-instrument dealer (Gebrauchtinstrumentenhandel), the instrument depot of a music school or orchestra, a brass band's rehearsal room or a reuse depot stores and offers it: the real standard instrument type of its period (student, orchestra and band models, DDR/BRD workshop classics as types, never brand names or logos) with real dimensions, scale lengths, materials and weights, cleaned and set up to be played again.

- **Category** is the one named in `assign.md`: `objects` (`S/🗂️catalog/🪑️objects`) for acoustic instruments, stands and cases, `appliances` (`S/🗂️catalog/🔌️appliances`) for everything that draws electrical power (amplifiers, stage pianos, organs, electronic drums, PA, mixers, turntables). Study the existing siblings first: `S/🗂️catalog/👤️humans/seated-guitarist` (a guitar on a body, its playing pose and the stool), objects `stepladder`, `storage-crate-stack`, `cooking-pot`, `chalkboard`, `shopping-trolley`; appliances `laptop`, `desktop-monitor`, `tower-server`, `pendant-lamp`, `vacuum-cleaner`; and, once published, the sibling wave's `used-upright-piano`.
- **Traces of use**, modelled as real geometry at the scales where they are above the smallest feature and as texture/detail strokes below: worn lacquer and varnish at the hand and chin contact points, finger wear on fretboards and keys, dented bells and bows, scratched ribs, rosin dust, tarnished plating, yellowed keys, torn tolex, dented heads, faded wraps, scuffed case corners, old stickers and repair cleats. Never damage that makes it unplayable: it is offered to be played again.
- **Storage state** as the default pose `stored`: how it really stands at the dealer or in the depot (in its case or gig bag, on an instrument stand, on a piano skid, laid on its side, drums nested in cases, under a cover, on a trolley), with case, stand, cover and trolley as parts of the asset on their own bones where they stay behind when the instrument is carried or played.
- **At least three poses**: `stored` (default), `carried` (in its case by the handle, on the back by straps, rolled on wheels or a trolley, by two or more people for heavy instruments; the carrying forces are supports at the grip anchors) and `played` (in its real playing position; the musician is not part of the asset, but the instrument stands, hangs or rests exactly where it does when played: on a stand, a stool, an endpin on the floor, a strap at shoulder height, with the playing forces of the hands, lips, chin or feet as loads at their anchors). Add poses the subject asks for (case open, lid open, assembled/disassembled, bellows open, extended stand).
- **At least two clips**: `carry` (stored → carried with root or part motion) and one clip of its playing life (bowing, strumming, valve or key cycle, slide motion, bellows, pedal tuning, strike and rebound of a drumhead or mallet, platter spin, case or lid opening, assembly).
- **Thermal**: every exposed surface a region with real material data (spruce, maple, rosewood, ebony, lacquer and varnish, brass and silver plating, nickel silver, steel strings, goat and calf skin, synthetic heads, felt, tolex, plywood, ABS, aluminium; aged surfaces differ from new ones — say so with a source tag). Metal instruments warm up in the hands and by the player's breath (moist warm air through the bore: model the breath as an emitter at the bell or the tone holes with its real temperature and humidity). Electrical equipment has `operating` keys, emitters and `ratedPowerW` with `ratedPowerBasis: "electrical-input"` (README section "Power"); acoustic instruments carry no rating or `passive` 0 W stated explicitly. Pose bindings exhaustive.
- **Structure**: the load path in each pose: floor, stand or case supports when stored, grip points when carried, the real supports and loads when played (string tension — a guitar about 0.7 kN, a violin about 0.25 kN, a piano about 180 kN on the frame —, endpin and stand reactions, strap and hand loads, pedal forces), members with real sections and materials, masses from section × density summing to `dimensions.massKg`.
- **Provenance**: `provenance.references` with organology literature (Hornbostel–Sachs class), standards and catalogue-typical data you used (cite precisely; tag parameters `literature`, `authored-estimate` or `illustrative` — nothing is `measured`). `tags` MUST include `"used"`, `"instrument"`, `"music"` and `"second-hand"` plus the family (`"strings"`, `"keyboard"`, `"woodwind"`, `"brass"`, `"percussion"`, `"folk"`, `"amplification"`, `"stage"`) and material/type tags. `summary` and every text `{ en, de }`, English first, German second, real sentences, no default language.

'''+s[b:]
